    "result_text": "The full suite is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipTier` field: **SILVER** when `namesakeCount` is 0 and an email is present, otherwise **BRONZE**.\n\nSince `membershipTier` is a purely derived read value (like the existing `displayName`/`initials`), I computed it in the mapper rather than storing it on the entity:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `membershipTier` property (enum `BRONZE`/`SILVER`) to the `Owner` response schema, which generates `OwnerDto.MembershipTierEnum`.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Mapping(... expression = \"java(toMembershipTier(owner))\")` on `toOwnerDto`, plus a `toMembershipTier` default method returning `SILVER` when `namesakeCount == 0` and email is non-blank, else `BRONZE` (null-safe on both fields, so seed/legacy owners without a namesake count fall through to `BRONZE`).\n\nThis flows through the existing `RespondWithOwner` step (and the create response), so both `GET /api/owners/{id}` and `POST /api/owners` return the tier. All tests pass (`Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`, BUILD SUCCESS).",
